Subject: [PATCH] llvm-profile: treat page release as a no-op on QNX

lprofReleaseMemoryPagesToOS() uses Linux-style madvise(MADV_DONTNEED),
which QNX does not provide (no madvise declaration; only the advisory
posix_madvise/POSIX_MADV_DONTNEED, which does not discard pages):

  InstrProfilingUtil.c:499: 'madvise' implicitly declared
  InstrProfilingUtil.c: 'MADV_DONTNEED' undeclared

The function is a pure RSS optimization: after continuous mode maps the
counters into the profile file, the original counter/bitmap pages are
released. Callers (InstrProfilingFile.c, InstrProfilingPlatformFuchsia.c)
ignore the result, and upstream already compiles it away on platforms
without madvise (VE, WASI). Extend that guard to QNX (__QNXNTO__).

---
--- a/src/llvm-project/compiler-rt/lib/profile/InstrProfilingUtil.c
+++ b/src/llvm-project/compiler-rt/lib/profile/InstrProfilingUtil.c
@@ -483,8 +483,10 @@ COMPILER_RT_VISIBILITY void lprofRestoreSigKill(void) {
 
 COMPILER_RT_VISIBILITY int lprofReleaseMemoryPagesToOS(uintptr_t Begin,
                                                        uintptr_t End) {
-#if defined(__ve__) || defined(__wasi__)
-  // VE and WASI doesn't support madvise.
+#if defined(__ve__) || defined(__wasi__) || defined(__QNXNTO__)
+  // VE and WASI don't support madvise. QNX has no Linux-style
+  // madvise(MADV_DONTNEED); releasing pages is only an RSS optimization,
+  // so treat it as a no-op like on VE/WASI.
   return 0;
 #else
   size_t PageSize = getpagesize();
